# Copy to ~/.config/llm-ask/aliases (or point LLM_ALIAS_FILE at it).
#
# Format: name = provider/slug — one per line, # starts a comment, trailing
# comments are stripped from the value.
#
# THIS FILE IS OPTIONAL, and increasingly unnecessary: `-m @top` picks the
# best-scored model straight from the catalogue, and `--top 5` shows you the
# ranking. Aliases are for pinning a deliberate choice — "always review with this
# one, so results stay comparable across weeks" — not for remembering slugs.
#
# No prices here on purpose: they move (three models changed rate within an hour
# during development). Ask the catalogue instead:
#
#   llm-ask.sh --top 5 --by coding
#   llm-ask.sh --list-models kimi
#
# The slugs below were live on 2026-08-18. Verify before trusting them.

# A stable pair for comparable week-to-week reviews.
reviewer   = openai/gpt-5.6-sol
reviewer-2 = moonshotai/kimi-k3

# Cheap runs, for iterating on the prompt rather than on the answer.
cheap      = openai/gpt-5.6-luna
